{% comment %}
  Section Wrapper
  Standard section container with consistent padding and max-width.

  Usage:
    {% render 'section-wrapper', id: section.id, class: 'my-section', bg: 'cream', inner_class: 'narrow' %}
      ... content ...
    {% endrender %}

  Since Liquid `render` doesn't support content blocks, use this pattern instead:

    <div class="section section--cream" id="section-{{ section.id }}">
      <div class="section__inner">
        ... content ...
      </div>
    </div>

  Parameters (for reference when building sections):
    - bg: 'white' | 'cream' | 'dark' | 'flush'
    - inner: 'default' | 'wide' | 'narrow' | 'copy'
    - padding: 'default' | 'narrow' | 'flush'
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  Since Liquid's `render` tag doesn't allow content blocks,
  this snippet documents the section wrapper pattern for consistency.

  STANDARD PATTERN (copy into each section):

  <section
    class="section{% if bg == 'cream' %} section--cream{% elsif bg == 'dark' %} section--dark{% endif %}{% if padding == 'narrow' %} section--narrow{% elsif padding == 'flush' %} section--flush{% endif %}"
    id="shopify-section-{{ section.id }}"
    {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <div class="section__inner{% if inner == 'wide' %} section__inner--wide{% elsif inner == 'narrow' %} section__inner--narrow{% endif %}">
      ... section content ...
    </div>
  </section>

  CSS classes available (from barreletics-base.css):
    .section              → default padding (64px/40px → 48px/16px mobile)
    .section--narrow      → reduced vertical padding (48px)
    .section--flush       → no padding
    .section--cream       → warm cream background (#f5f2ec)
    .section--dark        → charcoal background, white text
    .section__inner       → max-width 1200px centered
    .section__inner--wide → max-width 1400px
    .section__inner--narrow → max-width 760px
{% endcomment %}
